\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Lesion morphology. (a)~Malignant lesions are larger (median $\approx 12\%$ vs.\ $\approx 4\%$ of the image); many benign lesions are tiny. (b)~Malignant lesions are less circular/solid and more eccentric, i.e.\ more irregular. Both findings inform loss choice, model choice and the shape-feature experiment.}}{7}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:morph}{{3}{7}{Lesion morphology. (a)~Malignant lesions are larger (median $\approx 12\%$ vs.\ $\approx 4\%$ of the image); many benign lesions are tiny. (b)~Malignant lesions are less circular/solid and more eccentric, i.e.\ more irregular. Both findings inform loss choice, model choice and the shape-feature experiment}{figure.caption.9}{}}
